1
00:04:55,384 --> 00:05:01,384
No laws. No limits. One rule. Never fall in love.

2
00:09:50,769 --> 00:09:56,769
Moulin Rouge! is a drama, romance, music film directed by Baz Luhrmann.

3
00:14:46,153 --> 00:14:52,153
A celebration of love and creative inspiration takes place in the infamous, gaudy
and glamorous Parisian nightclub, at the cusp of the 20th century.

4
00:19:41,538 --> 00:19:47,538
A young poet, who is plunged into the heady world of Moulin Rouge, begins a
passionate affair with the club's most notorious and beautiful star.

5
00:24:36,923 --> 00:24:42,923
Christian, played by Ewan McGregor.

6
00:29:32,307 --> 00:29:38,307
Satine, played by Nicole Kidman.

7
00:34:27,692 --> 00:34:33,692
Toulouse-Lautrec, played by John Leguizamo.

8
00:39:23,076 --> 00:39:29,076
Harold Zidler, played by Jim Broadbent.

9
00:44:18,461 --> 00:44:24,461
The Duke, played by Richard Roxburgh.

10
00:49:13,846 --> 00:49:19,846
The Doctor, played by Garry McDonald.

11
00:54:09,230 --> 00:54:15,230
Moulin Rouge!

12
00:59:04,615 --> 00:59:10,615
(, French: [mulɛ̃ ʁuʒ]) is a 2001 jukebox musical romantic drama film
directed, produced, and co-written by Baz Luhrmann.

13
01:03:59,999 --> 01:04:05,999
It follows an English poet, Christian, who falls in love with the star of
the Moulin Rouge, cabaret actress and courtesan Satine.

14
01:08:55,384 --> 01:09:01,384
The film uses the musical setting of the Montmartre Quarter of Paris and is the final part of
Luhrmann's Red Curtain Trilogy, following Strictly Ballroom (1992) and Romeo + Juliet (1996).

15
01:13:50,769 --> 01:13:56,769
A co-production of Australia and the United States, it features an ensemble cast starring Nicole Kidman and Ewan McGregor,
with Jim Broadbent, Richard Roxburgh, John Leguizamo, Jacek Koman, and Caroline O'Connor in supporting roles.

16
01:18:46,153 --> 01:18:52,153
Moulin Rouge!

17
01:23:41,538 --> 01:23:47,538
premiered at the 2001 Cannes Film Festival, where it competed for the Palme d'Or and was
released in theaters on 25 May 2001 in Australia and on 1 June 2001 in North America.

18
01:28:36,923 --> 01:28:42,923
The film was praised for Luhrmann's direction, the performances of the
cast, its soundtrack, costume design, and production values.

19
01:33:32,307 --> 01:33:38,307
It was also a commercial success, grossing $179.2
million on a $50 million budget.

20
01:38:27,692 --> 01:38:33,692
At the 74th Academy Awards, the film received eight nominations, including Best
Picture, and won two (Best Production Design and Best Costume Design).

21
01:43:23,076 --> 01:43:29,076
Later critical reception for Moulin Rouge!

22
01:48:18,461 --> 01:48:24,461
remained positive and has been considered by many to be one of the best films of all time, with it
ranking 53rd in the BBC's 2016 poll of the 100 greatest films of the 21st century.

23
01:53:13,846 --> 01:53:19,846
A stage musical adaptation premiered in 2018.

24
01:58:09,230 --> 01:58:15,230
The film explores themes of paris, france, nightclub, fairy, courtesan, duke.

25
02:03:04,615 --> 02:03:10,615
The tone is emotional.
